<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Scheme
   LastUpgradeVersion = "2700"
   version = "1.7">
   <BuildAction
      parallelizeBuildables = "YES"
      buildImplicitDependencies = "YES"
      buildArchitectures = "Automatic">
      <BuildActionEntries>
         <BuildActionEntry
            buildForTesting = "YES"
            buildForRunning = "YES"
            buildForProfiling = "YES"
            buildForArchiving = "YES"
            buildForAnalyzing = "YES">
            <BuildableReference
               BuildableIdentifier = "primary"
               BlueprintIdentifier = "DF8513BC3027B5C400F0D2D5"
               BuildableName = "Hearth.app"
               BlueprintName = "Hearth Vision"
               ReferencedContainer = "container:Hearth.xcodeproj">
            </BuildableReference>
         </BuildActionEntry>
      </BuildActionEntries>
   </BuildAction>
   <TestAction
      buildConfiguration = "Debug"
      selectedDebuggerIdentifier = "Xcode.DebuggerFoundation.Debugger.LLDB"
      selectedLauncherIdentifier = "Xcode.DebuggerFoundation.Launcher.LLDB"
      shouldUseLaunchSchemeArgsEnv = "YES"
      shouldAutocreateTestPlan = "YES">
   </TestAction>
   <!--
      THE DEBUGGER IS OFF FOR RUN ON THIS SCHEME, deliberately, and this is the
      whole of the fix rather than half of it.

      An EMPTY selectedDebuggerIdentifier is Edit Scheme, Run, Info, "Debug
      executable" unchecked. Xcode builds, installs and launches; LLDB never
      attaches.

      The LAUNCHER stays LLDB and must. It is the thing that installs onto and
      starts a process on a remote device, and that is independent of whether a
      debugger then attaches. Setting it to
      Xcode.IDEFoundation.Launcher.PosixSpawn, which looks like the obvious
      partner for "no debugger" and is what Xcode writes for a Mac target, makes
      the scheme Mac only: every visionOS destination vanishes from the picker
      with no error saying why.

      Why nothing less works. The checkers below inject through
      DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES, and on a visionOS device the wedge is the injected
      dylib's load NOTIFICATION TO LLDB. The main thread hangs in dyld before
      main(), inside loadInsertedLibraries, registerInsertedLibrary,
      notifyDebuggerLoad, triggerNotifications. Disabling the checkers removes
      the dylibs but not the notify path, and with them off the observed symptom
      was still an endless "Configuring Debugger Actions" that cleared only by
      killing the app and launching it from the Home View. The resolution
      recorded in the Valinor client's visionos-crash-debug.md is exactly this:
      run without the debugger, and the app launches in about a second.

      The checkers stay disabled anyway, because they are what re-arms the trap
      the moment anyone ticks "Debug executable" back on to chase something.

      GPU validation and frame capture are off for the same reason, and are
      newer than the rest of this note: the target links Metal as of the face
      kernel, and frame capture AUTO-ENABLES for a Metal binary under the
      debugger. That is one more launch-time layer on the path that has already
      proven fragile here.

      WHAT THIS COSTS. No breakpoints, and print no longer reaches Xcode's
      console, because stdout is not the unified log. Everything worth reading
      on device therefore goes through os.Logger, which Console.app and
      "xcrun devicectl device console" both show with the debugger detached. To
      debug for real, tick "Debug executable" on and expect a slow first launch
      while LLDB builds its symbol cache.

      NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS COMMENT: no double hyphens. XML forbids them
      inside a comment, Xcode then fails to parse the whole scheme, and the
      symptom is an EMPTY destination picker rather than any kind of error.
   -->
   <LaunchAction
      buildConfiguration = "Debug"
      selectedDebuggerIdentifier = ""
      selectedLauncherIdentifier = "Xcode.DebuggerFoundation.Launcher.LLDB"
      launchStyle = "0"
      useCustomWorkingDirectory = "NO"
      ignoresPersistentStateOnLaunch = "NO"
      debugDocumentVersioning = "YES"
      debugServiceExtension = "internal"
      allowLocationSimulation = "YES"
      disableMainThreadChecker = "YES"
      disablePerformanceAntipatternChecker = "YES"
      enableGPUValidationMode = "1"
      enableGPUFrameCaptureMode = "3">
      <BuildableProductRunnable
         runnableDebuggingMode = "0">
         <BuildableReference
            BuildableIdentifier = "primary"
            BlueprintIdentifier = "DF8513BC3027B5C400F0D2D5"
            BuildableName = "Hearth.app"
            BlueprintName = "Hearth Vision"
            ReferencedContainer = "container:Hearth.xcodeproj">
         </BuildableReference>
      </BuildableProductRunnable>
   </LaunchAction>
   <ProfileAction
      buildConfiguration = "Release"
      shouldUseLaunchSchemeArgsEnv = "YES"
      savedToolIdentifier = ""
      useCustomWorkingDirectory = "NO"
      debugDocumentVersioning = "YES">
      <BuildableProductRunnable
         runnableDebuggingMode = "0">
         <BuildableReference
            BuildableIdentifier = "primary"
            BlueprintIdentifier = "DF8513BC3027B5C400F0D2D5"
            BuildableName = "Hearth.app"
            BlueprintName = "Hearth Vision"
            ReferencedContainer = "container:Hearth.xcodeproj">
         </BuildableReference>
      </BuildableProductRunnable>
   </ProfileAction>
   <AnalyzeAction
      buildConfiguration = "Debug">
   </AnalyzeAction>
   <ArchiveAction
      buildConfiguration = "Release"
      revealArchiveInOrganizer = "YES">
   </ArchiveAction>
</Scheme>
